From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anothers <14343424+Anothers@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 02:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 93/93] dsv41: retain 4K prefill workspace above retain floor
 with low-memory eviction

With TF_DSV41_PF_4K=1 and TF_DSV41_PREFILL=replay, cap sub-4,096 single
segments at min(seg, prefill_rows) via singleRows (and match ahead()
prefetching) so incremental tails hit AOT shapes instead of triggering
runtime Triton JIT stalls. Retain the ~2.3 GiB K4 workspace across
prompts only when all TP ranks agree MemAvailable >= retainFloorGiB()
(registered setting TF_DSV41_PF_WS_RETAIN_FLOOR_GIB, defaulting to
max(ws_floor + 1.0, target_floor + 1.5) = 6.5 GiB at prod floors, strictly
above admission and decode graph-capture floors).

Registers a low-memory eviction hook invoked by graphs.room() and
sched_host.admit() (retrying admission on mem_waits), re-checks memory in
wsAgreedWith even when retained, and maintains a symmetric TP collective
invariant (buf != null or evicted) so unilateral rank-0 eviction never
deadlocks TP=2 peers. Covered by host tests in review_workspace_test.zig.
